From a23bcabe90435ccb228620fbd80e5051c2ac8cfa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 12:28:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic: rtl8365mb: namiltd's RTL8367S-VB (family D) series,
 PR #19644

Local copy of the family-D series at commit cc4e2b217, which is now the
head of BOTH namiltd/openwrt#134 and openwrt/openwrt#19644 - the work
moved into the upstream-facing PR and the patch files were renamed to the
descriptive form.

Change since the 2026-08-27 drop, and it looks like the fix for what the
tester saw: the family-D SerDes tuning table is now written through the
SDS13 indirect window (new rtl8365mb_sds_write_index() plus
RTL8365MB_D_SDS_EXT0_INDEX = 13) instead of index 0. Previously the mode
bits reached the right register while the tuning went to the wrong
SerDes, which matches the report of a 2.5G link that negotiates but
passes no traffic.

Verified with target/linux/prepare against the builder's own upstream
base (ax55-618-rebase @785c2661d6, kernel 6.18.39, TESTING_KERNEL=y):
EXIT 0, all seven applied, RTL8367S-VB/0x6642 and the SDS13 index present
in the prepared source.
